thy algebraic\n   manipulation) gives the compact expression  \n\n   \\[\n   O=H+\\alpha\\,\\mathbf v^{\\perp},\n   \\qquad \n   \\alpha=\\frac{\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}}\n                {2\\bigl((A-N)\\times\\mathbf v\\bigr)} .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n   Formula (6) shows immediately that  \n\n   \\[\n   (O-H)\\cdot\\mathbf v=0,\n   \\]\n   i.e. the segment \\(OH\\) is perpendicular to the direction \\(\\mathbf v\\) of\n   \\(AP\\).\n\n7. **Equality of the radius.**  \n   From (6),\n\n   \\[\n   |O-H|^{2}= \\alpha^{2}\\,\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}. \\tag{7}\n   \\]\n\n   Computing \\(|O-B|^{2},|O-E|^{2},|O-F|^{2}\\) with the same formula (6) and\n   using the defining relations  \n\n   \\[\n   x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=r^{2},\\qquad (x_{0}-d)^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=R^{2},\n   \\]\n   one obtains exactly the same expression \\(\\alpha^{2}\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}\\).\n   Hence  \n\n   \\[\n   |O-H|^{2}=|O-B|^{2}=|O-E|^{2}=|O-F|^{2}.\n   \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n\n   Consequently the common value \\(\\rho:=|O-H|\\) is the radius of the\n   circumcircle \\((O,\\rho)\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n8. **Tangency.**  \n   The line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is  \n\n   \\[\n   \\ell:\\;(x,y)=H+t\\mathbf v,\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb R .\n   \\]\n\n   Because of (6) the radius \\(OH\\) is orthogonal to the direction \\(\\mathbf v\\);\n   therefore \\(\\ell\\) is perpendicular to the radius at the point \\(H\\).\n   By (8) the distance from \\(O\\) to \\(\\ell\\) equals the radius \\(\\rho\\);\n   hence \\(\\ell\\) meets the circle \\((O,\\rho)\\) in exactly one point.\n   Thus \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Conclusion** – The line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The required line is tangent to the circumcircle of } \\triangle BEF.}\n\\]\n\n### Your Attack ###\nTry HA