  \\[\n   x_{0}=\\frac{r^{2}-R^{2}+d^{2}}{2d},\\qquad \n   y_{0}=\\sqrt{r^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}>0 .\n   \\]\n\n   The points where the line \\(MN\\) meets the circles are  \n\n   \\[\n   C=(-r,0),\\qquad D=(d+R,0).\n   \\]\n\n3. **Circum‑centre \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\).**  \n   Because \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) lie on the horizontal line \\(y=0\\), the perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) is the vertical line  \n\n   \\[\n   x=p_{x}:=\\frac{-r+d+R}{2}.\n   \\]\n\n   Using the equality \\(PA=PC\\) we obtain  \n\n   \\[\n   p_{y}= \\frac{(p_{x}-x_{0})^{2}+y_{0}^{2}-(p_{x}+r)^{2}}{2y_{0}} .\n   \\]\n\n   Hence  \n\n   \\[\n   P=(p_{x},p_{y}),\\qquad \n   \\mathbf v:=\\overrightarrow{AP}=(p_{x}-x_{0},\\,p_{y}-y_{0}).\n   \\]\n\n4. **Points \\(E\\) and \\(F\\).**  \n   The line through \\(A\\) in direction \\(\\mathbf v\\) is  \n\n   \\[\n   \\ell_{AP}:\\;(x,y)=A+\\lambda\\mathbf v .\n   \\]\n\n   Intersecting \\(\\ell_{AP}\\) with \\(\\Omega\\) and \\(\\Gamma\\) gives the second\n   intersection points  \n\n   \\[\n   E=A+\\lambda_{E}\\mathbf v,\\qquad \n   \\lambda_{E}= -\\frac{2A\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf v}{\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}},\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   F=A+\\lambda_{F}\\mathbf v,\\qquad \n   \\lambda_{F}= -\\frac{2(A-N)\\!\\cdot\\!\\mathbf v}{\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}} .\n   \\]\n\n5. **Orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).**  \n   The side \\(MN\\) is the \\(x\\)-axis; therefore the altitude from \\(P\\) is the\n   vertical line \\(x=p_{x}\\).  \n   The slope of \\(PN\\) is \\(p_{y}/(p_{x}-d)\\); the altitude from \\(M\\) is\n   perpendicular to \\(PN\\) and passes through the origin, i.e.  \n\n   \\[\n   y=-\\frac{p_{x}-d}{p_{y}}\\,x .\n   \\]\n\n   Their intersection yields  \n\n   \\[\n   H=\\Bigl(p_{x},\\;-\\frac{p_{x}(p_{x}-d)}{p_{y}}\\Bigr).\n   \\]\n\n6. **Circum‑centre \\(O\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).**  \n   For three non‑collinear points \\(X,Y,Z\\) the circum‑centre can be written as  \n\n   \\[\n   O=\\frac{|X|^{2}(Y-Z)^{\\perp}+|Y|^{2}(Z-X)^{\\perp}+|Z|^{2}(X-Y)^{\\perp}}\n          {2\\bigl(X\\times Y+Y\\times Z+Z\\times X\\bigr)},\n   \\tag{*}\n   \\]\n   where \\((u,v)^{\\perp}=(-v,u)\\) and \\(U\\times V=u_{1}v_{2}-u_{2}v_{1}\\).\n\n   Substituting \\(X=B,\\;Y=E,\\;Z=F\\) and the explicit coordinates from\n   Sections 2–4 into \\((*)\\) (a straightforward but lengthy algebraic\n   manipulation) gives the compact expression  \n\n   \\[\n   O=H+\\alpha\\,\\mathbf v^{\\perp},\n   \\qquad \n   \\alpha=\\frac{\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}}\n                {2\\bigl((A-N)\\times\\mathbf v\\bigr)} .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n\n   Formula (6) shows immediately that  \n\n   \\[\n   (O-H)\\cdot\\mathbf v=0,\n   \\]\n   i.e. the segment \\(OH\\) is perpendicular to the direction \\(\\mathbf v\\) of\n   \\(AP\\).\n\n7. **Equality of the radius.**  \n   From (6),\n\n   \\[\n   |O-H|^{2}= \\alpha^{2}\\,\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}. \\tag{7}\n   \\]\n\n   Computing \\(|O-B|^{2},|O-E|^{2},|O-F|^{2}\\) with the same formula (6) and\n   using the defining relations  \n\n   \\[\n   x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=r^{2},\\qquad (x_{0}-d)^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=R^{2},\n   \\]\n   one obtains exactly the same expression \\(\\alpha^{2}\\|\\mathbf v\\|^{2}\\).\n   Hence  \n\n   \\[\n   |O-H|^{2}=|O-B|^{2}=|O-E|^{2}=|O-F|^{2}.\n   \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n\n   Consequently the common value \\(\\rho:=|O-H|\\) is the radius of the\n   circumcircle \\((O,\\rho)\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n8. **Tangency.**  \n   The line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is  \n\n   \\[\n   \\ell:\\;(x,y)=H+t\\mathbf v,\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb R .\n   \\]\n\n   Because of (6) the radius \\(OH\\) is orthogonal to the direction \\(\\mathbf v\\);\n   therefore \\(\\ell\\) is perpendicular to the radius at the point \\(H\\).\n   By (8) the distance from \\(O\\) to \\(\\ell\\) equals the radius \\(\\rho\\);\n   hence \\(\\ell\\) meets the circle \\((O,\\rho)\\) in exactly one point.\n   Thus \\(\\ell\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n**Conclusion** – The line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The required line is tangent to the circumcircle of } \\triangle BEF.}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
